# Review ownership.
#
# One maintainer owns everything, which makes the catch-all rule honest rather
# than decorative. The specific rules below exist so that when a second person
# arrives, the boundaries are already drawn where they matter rather than
# being invented under time pressure.

*                       @FrancoisLDaigneault

# Anything that decides what "correct" means. A change here changes every
# repository's definition of a passing build.
/.github/workflows/     @FrancoisLDaigneault
/.pre-commit-config.yaml @FrancoisLDaigneault
/clippy.toml            @FrancoisLDaigneault
/deny.toml              @FrancoisLDaigneault
/rust-toolchain.toml    @FrancoisLDaigneault

# Recorded decisions. Editing one is not the same as editing code, and a
# review of an ADR is a review of the reasoning rather than the diff.
/docs/adr/              @FrancoisLDaigneault
